title: Stèlegraphy
message: >-
  If you use this software in work you publish, please cite it using the
  metadata in this file.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Kevin
    family-names: Praditiansyah
    email: kevinpradithh@gmail.com
    website: https://www.linkedin.com/in/kevinpradith/
repository-code: https://github.com/kevinpradith/stelegraphy
url: https://stelegraphy.kevinpradith.my.id
abstract: >-
  A browser application that turns text into Elder Futhark runes and back. The
  transform is a repeating-key XOR over URI-encoded text, normalised through
  Base64 and mapped one-to-one onto 64 runes, so it is a Vigenere cipher over
  bytes and is documented as such: the repository names the known-plaintext,
  Kasiski and brute-force attacks that recover the key rather than describing
  the output as encryption. Everything runs in the tab, with no network request
  and a Content-Security-Policy that forbids one. It is intended as a teaching
  example of the distance between text that looks secret and text that is.
keywords:
  - cipher
  - xor
  - vigenere
  - elder-futhark
  - cryptography-education
  - client-side
  - nextjs
  - typescript
